note Values go straight into text: put a variable or a calculation in brackets.
name = "Ada"
score = 41
ask "Hello (name), what is your favourite number?" store as favourite

print "Hi (name)! Your score is (score), next is (score + 1)."
print "Your favourite number doubled is (favourite * 2)."
print "(name) has (length of name) letters."

note Brackets that are not variables are printed as written:
print "Are you ready? (yes or no)"
print "Press (1) to start"

note Use a backslash to keep a bracket that would be filled in:
print "Type \(name) to see the name"
